    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56641": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor in Kinesiology",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor in Kinesiology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor in Kinesiology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Lecturer or Teaching Assistant Professor in Kinesiology Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Lecturer/Teaching Assistant Professor Position Number 064501 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Kinesiology - 273200 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Earned Master’s degree or Doctoral degree in Kinesiology or a closely related discipline. Candidates whose degree is in a related discipline must demonstrate academic experience to be considered applicable for designation as Kinesiology faculty. Experience in a Strength and Conditioning setting as a coach or other applied practitioner, and current CSCS certification. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Demonstrated potential to provide effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level in strength and conditioning-related courses. Demonstrated teaching expertise in one or more of the following areas: theoretical aspects of strength and conditioning, applied aspects of strength and conditioning, sport science, sport nutrition USAW , CPSS , or other relevant credential Experience with CASCE accreditation requirements Evidence of ability to mentor students in career advancement in the strength and conditioning field Evidence of service to the university, community, and/or professional organizations License/Certification Required CSCS ( NSCA ) Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Kinesiology within the Beaver College of Health Sciences comprises nationally accredited and recognized programs, including a Bachelor of Science and Master of Science degree in Kinesiology (formerly Exercise Science). The Kinesiology graduate program at App State has a long history of success and prestige in strength & conditioning and clinical exercise physiology. The department features state-of-the-art laboratories and supports faculty with diverse research and practice backgrounds. Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through inclusive practices, interprofessional collaboration, and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Kinesiology program within the Strength and Conditioning concentration (3:3 teaching load). Serving as the Field Experience Coordinator for undergraduate and graduate CASCE -accredited S&C concentrations comprises the remainder of the teaching load each semester. Participating in service activities for the department, university, community, and professional organizations. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 FTE Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position Ability to demonstrate weight training exercises and sport performance drills. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/09/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide: Letter of Interest CV Professional Reference List Unofficial Transcripts A document of Teaching Philosophy A document describing strength and conditioning practical/coaching experience UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/16/2026 Closing Date 10/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/16/2026 Search Chair Name N. Travis Triplett Search Chair Email triplttnt@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55951 Posting Number FA00605P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Miscellaneous (Explanation in Applicant Instructions) Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
