    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56441": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Library &amp; Information Science",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant or Associate Professor of Library &amp; Information Science Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant or Associate Professor of Library & Information Science Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Library & Information Science Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant or Associate Professor Position Number 092311 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Leadership, Library and Information Science, and Research - 260300 Working Location (City, State) Remote (must be within driving distance to Boone, NC) Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications ALA -accredited MLIS degree or equivalent advanced degree (Need to submit degree/official transcript by the first day of employment) A doctorate degree, or ABD with completion date by Sept. 1, at the time of appointment in Library and Information Science, or a related field Online teaching experience at the graduate or undergraduate level Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Capacity to work with students specializing in areas across LIS disciplines Defined research agenda Areas of interest might include the following: information behavior, information retrieval, human-information interaction, data science, artificial intelligence, human-centered computing, information management, knowledge organization, information visualization, digital scholarship, information policy, digital stewardship, or related areas Excellent written and oral communication skills and the ability to communicate with a broad group of individuals Excellent organization and time management skills Familiarity with current LMS platforms (preferably Canvas) Evidence of a current or emerging research agenda related to library and information science Experience with assessment and accreditation Ability to manage competing priorities in a collaborative environment while fostering a welcoming and respectful atmosphere Record of service to organization or profession Ability to teach Organization of Information Experience in information science License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit Department of Leadership, Library and Information Science, and Research Essential Duties and Responsibilities Position Context The Library and Information Science program at Appalachian State University prepares students to pursue careers in libraries or information fields. The Program has achieved Pre-Candidacy Accreditation status from the American Library Association ( ALA ): View Program retention and graduation data .The Master of Library and Information Science ( MLIS ) is a 36-credit hour online degree program that prepares students to foster digital and information literacies, assist underserved populations, and bridge the gap between people, information, and technology. The program’s curriculum has been developed and is reviewed annually to ensure that it enables students to successfully meet the program’s Learning Objectives. Granted Precandidacy Accreditation Status from the American Library Association Growing program Core Position Responsibilities Teach graduate courses in Library and Information Science at the master’s level, 18 credit hours, which corresponds to six courses during the academic year. Curriculum and course development, especially in areas of information science. Contribute to the development, implementation, and ongoing assessment of the MLIS programs. Advise and mentor graduate students. Engage in scholarly activity appropriate for tenure and promotion, including research, publication, and/or grant activity related to Library and Information Science. Contribute to accreditation, assessment, and continuous improvement efforts within the Library and Information Science Program. Participate in service through committee work, professional engagement, and community partnerships. Connect the program with emerging information professions. Collaborate with faculty across academic units on interdisciplinary teaching, research, and grant initiatives. Engage in an active program of scholarship and professional service to the MLIS Program, the Department, the University, and/or the public, including committee work as specified in the University’s Faculty Handbook. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 07/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Will consider ABD with completion date by Sept. 1. For a complete application, please apply and submit all required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: A cover letter addressing the candidate’s qualifications A Curriculum Vita Unofficial Graduate/Doctoral Transcripts A statement of teaching philosophy A statement of research agenda (included as research interest attachment) A list of three professional References with contact information UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/15/2026 Search Chair Name Alex McAllister Search Chair Email mcallisterad@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56251 Posting Number FA00612P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56424": {
      "title": "DNP Family Nurse Practitioner Program Faculty",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | DNP Family Nurse Practitioner Program Faculty Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources DNP Family Nurse Practitioner Program Faculty Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title DNP Family Nurse Practitioner Program Faculty Tenure Status Provide Rank Open Rank Position Number 0A1191 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Department of Nursing - 273300 Working Location (City, State) Hickory, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Earned nursing-related doctoral degree from an accredited institution by the time of appointment* One graduate degree must be in nursing (master’s or doctorate) Minimum 2 years of experience as nurse practitioner National certiﬁcation as a nurse practitioner *We will review application materials from and interview candidates who have not yet completed their doctorate—are “ABD”—but they must complete this requirement and earn the doctorate by July 31, 2027 Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Excellent communication, interpersonal, and collaboration skills. Knowledge of curriculum and curriculum development Ability to think creatively and strategically Candidates with experience in these areas are encouraged to apply: primary care, reproductive health and/or pediatrics. A commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship, compatible with the BCHS mission License/Certification Required Possess (or be eligible for) current registered nurse license and hold or be eligible for licensure as a nurse practitioner in the state of North Carolina; current national certiﬁcation as a Nurse Practitioner (NP); meet the North Carolina Board of Nursing’s requirements for nurse educators within 3 years of employment. Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Nursing within the Beaver College of Health Sciences was founded in 2007 and offers a pre-licensure BSN , the online RN to BSN , and MSN programs with a concentration in nursing education, and a DNP Family Nurse Practitioner program established in 2026. The BSN , RN to BSN , and MSN programs are fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education ( CCNE ); the DNP program holds new applicant status with CCNE . The department features state-of-the-art laboratories and supports faculty with varying research and practice backgrounds. Learn more at https://nursing.appstate.edu/ Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through dynamic practices, interprofessional collaboration, and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,900 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu Essential Duties and Responsibilities This posting is for one or more Open Rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) Faculty member position(s) – rank to be determined by the Department of Nursing in conjunction with the Dean of the College prior to an offer being made to any candidate. The purpose of the position is to provide instruction in the DNP FNP program. This may include teaching in the classroom, clinical settings, simulation, or online. The faculty is responsible for collaboration with colleagues and students, for maintaining the quality of the academic curriculum through development, implementation, and evaluation; contributing to accreditation work and program evaluation; student recruitment, admissions and progression; and student advisement. As a member of the faculty, the individual will be expected to contribute to teaching, practice, scholarship, and service, including participation in oﬃcial activities of the department, college, and university, among others. This position is based on the Appalachian State University Hickory Campus. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 FTE Number Of Months Per Year 11 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/14/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide with your application the following documents: Letter of Interest, Curriculum Vitae, Professional Reference List, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, Statement of Research Interests, and Unofficial Transcripts We will review application materials from and interview candidates who have not yet completed their doctorate—are “ABD”—but they must complete this requirement and earn the doctorate by July 31, 2027 UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date 11/29/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/30/2026 Search Chair Name Gregory Marler Search Chair Email marlergs@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56215 Posting Number FA00611P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Letter of Interest Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Transcript-Associate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
