    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56324": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 010391 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Physics & Astronomy - 250700 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Physics, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Materials Engineering, or a related field. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Candidates with research experience in nanoscience, advanced materials, and nanoscale imaging and characterization are encouraged to apply. License/Certification Required Description of the Department or Unit The department offers a B.A. and a B.S. in Physics with multiple concentrations , including a B.S. in Physics with a concentration in Secondary Education . Additionally, the department’s M.S. program in Engineering Physics is a national leader in instrumentation and automation. The faculty includes 16 TT and 12 full-time NTT members. Both undergraduate and graduate programs are consistently ranked among the largest in the country by the AIP when compared to other Masters granting institutions: enrollment exceeds 170 undergraduate majors and 20+ graduate students. Appalachian is one of 17 campuses in the University of North Carolina System; it enrolls more than 21,000 students, has a low student-to-faculty ratio, and offers more than 150 undergraduate and graduate programs. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Candidates must have a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate education and are expected to teach in and make significant contributions to the M.S. program in Engineering Physics , including the concentration in Nanoscience for Advanced Materials . Candidates with research experience in nanoscience, advanced materials, and nanoscale imaging and characterization are encouraged to apply. Candidates are expected to develop a research program that, in addition to involving undergraduate and M.S. students, can attract external funding, develop collaborations with departmental faculty, and utilize facilities and equipment within the department. Candidates with an interest in developing industry and/or agency connections are encouraged to apply. Start-up funds and laboratory space will be available to the successful candidate. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants To apply please submit the following application materials: (1) a cover letter delineating your interests and qualifications, (2) a description of your research program that includes how you will implement it at Appalachian State, and how you will involve and mentor undergraduate and M.S. students, (3) a description of your teaching philosophy that includes how you will contribute to introductory or advanced undergraduate courses, and to Master’s level courses in our programs, (4) a curriculum vitae that clearly highlights work relevant to this position, (5) a list of three references, and (6) an artificial intelligence (AI) disclosure statement that clearly states if and how AI was used in the development of the application materials. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/23/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 11/16/2026 Search Chair Name Chris Thaxton Search Chair Email coffeyts@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56129 Posting Number FA00608P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Miscellaneous (Explanation in Applicant Instructions) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56267": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences)",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Psychology (Personality and Individual Differences) Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 018531 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Psychology - 250800 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field by the starting date. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Prefer expertise in Personality and Individual Differences. The area of specialization within Personality Psychology is open. Applicants whose primary area of specialization is outside Personality will be considered, as long as they demonstrate knowledge of and competence in the field of Personality Psychology. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department has 43 full-time faculty members (33 tenure-track) with graduate programs in Clinical, Psychological Science, Industrial-Organizational and Human Resource Management, and School Psychology. There are more than 1400 undergraduate majors and nearly 100 full-time graduate students. Additional information about the Department of Psychology is located on the Psychology Department website . Essential Duties and Responsibilities The candidate will be expected to teach an undergraduate course in Personality and Individual Differences, in addition to other courses, according to need and/or interest (e.g., Psychology of Personality, Personality Laboratory, Contemporary Issues in Psychology). The successful candidate will be expected to establish a program of empirical research, including peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and external grant applications. They will also be expected to involve undergraduate and graduate students in their research programs and may affiliate with any of the Department’s four graduate programs. Preference will be given to candidates with a commitment to undergraduate education and the ability to involve undergraduate and graduate students in their program of research. The successful candidate will teach three courses per semester, which might include a combination of undergraduate and graduate courses. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 07/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: A cover letter addressing the candidate’s qualifications for the Assistant Professor position in Personality and Individual Differences A Curriculum Vita Unofficial Graduate Transcripts A statement of teaching philosophy, interests, and evidence of teaching effectiveness that includes which courses from the Undergraduate Psychology Bulletin you would be able to teach A statement of research interests and research plans for the next 3 years A list of three professional References with contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later date. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Chris Dickinson Search Chair Email dickinsonca@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/54387 Posting Number FA00585P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56264": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders / Speech-Language Pathology",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders / Speech-Language Pathology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders / Speech-Language Pathology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor in Communication Sciences and Disorders / Speech-Language Pathology Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant / Associate Professor Position Number 019941 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Rehabilitation Sciences - 273100 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences is searching for an Assistant/Associate Professors specializing in Communication Sciences and Disorders/Speech-Language Pathology. An earned doctoral degree in speech-language pathology or related area is required. ABD applications will be considered with initial appointment at the rank of Instructor. All degree requirements must be completed by February 28, 2028 for subsequent appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Applications are encouraged from all qualified candidates. Applications are particularly encouraged from candidates with expertise in the areas of child language disorders, autism, literacy, cultural-linguistic variations, and/or complex communication needs. For appointments at the rank of Assistant Professor, candidates must demonstrate the potential for effective teaching, student mentoring, and conducting research in the area of expertise. For appointments at the rank of Associate Professor, candidates must demonstrate a history of successful teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels, student mentoring, research productivity, and academic/professional service. License/Certification Required Ideal candidates will be eligible for the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association ( ASHA ) Certificate of Clinical Competence and North Carolina licensure Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences within the Beaver College of Health Sciences includes fully accredited graduate programs in Athletic Training, Speech-Language Pathology, and Occupational Therapy, an undergraduate program in Communication Sciences and Disorders, and minors in American Sign Language and Communication Sciences and Disorders. Our students are trained to empower people of all ages to improve/restore their functional abilities, fulfill their daily routines and roles, mitigate limitations or disabilities following injury or illness, and live full lives in the context of differing abilities. In addition, the department is home to the Charles and Geneva S. Scott Scottish Rite Communication Disorders Clinic, which provides speech-language pathology, audiology, and pediatric occupational therapy services as an outreach to the community and serves as a primary site for student clinical training. Department of Rehabilitation Sciences graduates transition into their respective positions as qualified healthcare practitioners with enhanced clinical skills, knowledge, and values. They will be well-prepared to improve the health and wellness of people across the region, state, and world. The department emphasizes interprofessional education, clinical-academic collaboration, and academic excellence. Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through interprofessional collaboration and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, both face-to-face and online, conducting research and seeking external funding, and engaging in university and professional service. Opportunities for direct clinical service and clinical supervision may also be available. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 FTE Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/09/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide with your application the following documents: Letter of Interest, Curriculum Vitae, Professional Reference List, Statement of Teaching Philosophy, Statement of Research Interests, and Unofficial Transcripts ABD applications will be considered with an initial appointment at the rank of Instructor. All degree requirements must be completed by February 28, 2028 for subsequent appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 12/01/2026 Search Chair Name Dr. Stefan Frisch Search Chair Email frischsa@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56118 Posting Number FA00606P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56166": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Education",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Director of Clinical Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Director of Clinical Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Director of Clinical Education Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor Position Number 004301 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Rehabilitation Sciences - 273100 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution. Current ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology ( CCC - SLP ). Current North Carolina licensure in Speech-Language Pathology or eligibility to obtain North Carolina licensure upon hire. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) The department is seeking a faculty member with both clinical and academic experience who has a strong desire to foster clinical education for students and to connect students to professionals in the community for advanced clinical experiences. Candidates should possess: Demonstrated competence in clinical practice. Demonstrated ability to effectively carry out teaching and educational responsibilities. Ability to contribute to the department’s clinical, professional, and service needs. License/Certification Required ASHA CCC and NC State Licensure in Speech-Language Pathology (or qualifications to immediately apply). Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences within Beaver College of Health Sciences includes fully accredited graduate programs in Athletic Training, Speech-Language Pathology, and Occupational Therapy, an undergraduate program in Communication Sciences and Disorders, and minors in American Sign Language and Communication Sciences and Disorders. Our students are trained to empower people of all ages to improve/restore their functional abilities, fulfill their daily routines and roles, mitigate limitations or disabilities following injury or illness, and live full lives in the context of differing abilities. In addition, the department is home to the Charles and Geneva S. Scott Scottish Rite Communication Disorders Clinic, which provides speech-language pathology, audiology, and pediatric occupational therapy services as an outreach to the community and serves as a primary site for student clinical training. Department of Rehabilitation Sciences graduates transition into their respective positions as qualified healthcare practitioners with enhanced clinical skills, knowledge, and values. They will be well-prepared to improve the health and wellness of people across the region, state, and world. The department emphasizes interprofessional education, clinical-academic collaboration, and academic excellence. For more information, go to https://rhs.appstate.edu/ Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through interprofessional collaboration and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu Essential Duties and Responsibilities The SLP Director of Clinical Education will develop, implement, manage, and evaluate clinical education for the department’s graduate Speech-Language Pathology and undergraduate Communication Sciences and Disorders programs. The SLP Director of Clinical Education will also provide administrative leadership for the department’s three clinical units (two on-campus and one in Hickory) which include seven speech-language pathologists and one occupational therapist. This individual will also establish, maintain, and grow off-campus clinical placements. There is also an opportunity for academic teaching. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 12-month Leave Earning Faculty Contract Physical Demands of Position Travel between clinic locations, as well as to off-campus clinic sites, and meet with faculty, students and community professionals to manage and promote clinical education. To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide with your application the following documents: Letter of Interest, Curriculum Vitae, Professional Reference List and Unofficial Transcripts UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/15/2026 Closing Date 10/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/30/2026 Search Chair Name Gary McCullough Search Chair Email mcculloughgh@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55968 Posting Number FA00604P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56146": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Construction Management, or Engineering Experience (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Construction Management, or Engineering Experience (Multiple Vacancies) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Construction Management, or Engineering Experience (Multiple Vacancies) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Construction Management, or Engineering Experience (Multiple Vacancies) Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 083281, 0A0321, 098761 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Sustain Tech & Built Envir - 265300 Working Location (City, State) Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications An Earned Doctorate in Construction, Civil Engineering, or Architecture is required by the time of hire; closely related fields may be considered. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Sustainable Technology & the Built Environment ( STBE ) houses three academic programs: the Bachelor of Science (BS) in Renewable Energy Technology; the BS in Building Sciences, with two concentrations; and the Master of Science in Technology. The Department includes more than 35 full-time faculty serving approximately 950 undergraduate and 30 graduate students. STBE has played an integral role in building the University’s sustainability agenda, which features prominently in the University’s Strategic Plan. Within STBE , faculty exemplify a commitment to applied research and interdisciplinary, experiential learning. Students in these programs have achieved notable successes in national and international competitions such as the Formula Sun Grand Prix and American Solar Challenge, the USDOE Race to Zero and Solar Decathlon, Solar Decathlon Europe, and the US EPA P3 program, among others. The Building Sciences Program is structured to establish a broad set of foundational skills and knowledge related to the whole life cycle of the built environment, including design, construction, and operations. This foundation acts as a catalyst for growth and success in our graduates’ careers. Extending beyond foundational principles, the program is committed to priming students’ minds to deconstruct, organize, and solve a wide range of problems related to the built environment in a team-based setting. Students go on to career paths in architecture, construction, building performance assessment, and facilities management. The College of Fine and Applied Arts ( CFAA ) at Appalachian State University is a dynamic, transdisciplinary academic unit that emphasizes experiential learning and offers 30 undergraduate degree programs, one graduate degree program and 13 minors through its seven member departments: Applied Design; Art; Communication; Military Science and Leadership; Sustainable Development; Sustainable Technology and the Built Environment; and Theatre and Dance (https://cfaa.appstate.edu/). Essential Duties and Responsibilities The primary responsibility of the position is teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Building Sciences program, which may include but are not limited to: 1. Construction Management Techniques 2. Engineering and Construction Education 3. Sustainable Building Design and Construction 4. Building Science 5. Virtual Design and Construction 6. Automation in Construction 7. Materials and Structures Other responsibilities include maintaining an active scholarly agenda, team-based coordination of a four-course studio sequence or building sciences integrated courses, advising students, collaborating with professionals in the building industry, and participating in service work. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position Typical physical demands of classroom and educational environments in a professional position at a university. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: ● Cover Letter / Letter of Interest that includes the following brief statements: Philosophy of instructional design Scholarly interests Commitment to sustainability ● Curriculum Vitae ● Sample of Architectural Design and/or Research Projects and/or Teaching Portfolio (max six pages) ● Unofficial Graduate Transcript(s) ● List of at least three (3) References with Contact Information ● Optional: License/Certification UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Sharareh Shirzad Search Chair Email shirzads@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55817 Posting Number FA00602P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Sample Projects (Explanation in Applicant Instructions) Optional Documents License/Certification Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56127": {
      "title": "Open Rank of Occupational Therapy (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor)",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Open Rank of Occupational Therapy (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Open Rank of Occupational Therapy (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Open Rank of Occupational Therapy (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant / Associate / Full Professor / BCBS Distinguished Professorship Position Number 091451 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Rehabilitation Sciences - 273100 Working Location (City, State) Boone, NC Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications An earned terminal doctoral degree in occupational therapy or occupational science, or an entry-level degree in occupational therapy combined with a doctoral degree in a related field A minimum of three years of practice experience in occupational therapy Training or experience demonstrating the potential for effective teaching, student mentoring, and conducting research in the area of expertise Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Appalachian State University’s Master of Science in Occupational Therapy ( MSOT ) program was accredited by the Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education ( ACOTE ) in May 2026 and recently graduated its first cohort of students. The program seeks an experienced faculty member with established expertise, leadership, and scholarly perspective to join a collegial academic community committed to excellence in occupational therapy education, meaningful scholarship, and service to the profession and surrounding communities. As a faculty member, this individual will have opportunities to help shape the continued growth and direction of the occupational therapy program, mentor students and faculty, advance an established program of scholarship, and build interdisciplinary and community partnerships across the Beaver College of Health Sciences, the University, and region. Appalachian State University is classified as a Research 2- Doctoral University, characterized by high research spending and doctorate production by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education and has expanding opportunities for research and innovation. For appointments at the rank of Associate Professor, candidates must demonstrate a documented record of effective teaching, student mentoring, and independent research in the area of expertise as evidenced by scholarly dissemination and pursuit of funding. For appointments at the rank of Full Professor or Blue Cross Blue Shield of North Carolina Distinguished Professor, candidates must meet all departmental, university, and college requirements for appointment with tenure, including demonstrating a documented history of exemplary teaching, successful mentoring of students and other faculty, institutional and professional service, and an established program of research including dissemination and extramural funding. Candidates at this rank are also anticipated to have a record of successful mentoring of other faculty. Highly qualified candidates whose experience and credentials demonstrate the capacity to provide leadership and vision will be considered for the Blue Cross Blue Shield of NC Distinguished Professorship. Competitive candidates will present: A minimum of 5 years of experience in an occupational therapy educational program with a focus on student-and subject-centered pedagogy Strong record of mentorship of both students and faculty Evidence of an independent and sustained line of research License/Certification Required Initial national board certification as an occupational therapist. Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in North Carolina, USA Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences , within the Beaver College of Health Sciences , includes fully accredited graduate programs in Athletic Training, Speech-Language Pathology, and Occupational Therapy, an undergraduate program in Communication Sciences and Disorders, and minors in American Sign Language and Communication Sciences and Disorders. Our students are trained to empower people of all ages to improve/restore their functional abilities, fulfill their daily routines and roles, mitigate limitations or disabilities following injury or illness, and live full lives in the context of differing abilities. In addition, the department is home to the Charles and Geneva S. Scott Scottish Rite Communication Disorders Clinic, which provides speech-language pathology, audiology, and pediatric occupational therapy services as an outreach to the community and serves as a primary site for student clinical training. Department of Rehabilitation Sciences graduates transition into their respective positions as qualified healthcare practitioners with enhanced clinical skills, knowledge, and values. They will be well-prepared to improve the health and wellness of people across the region, state, and world. The department emphasizes interprofessional education, clinical-academic collaboration, and academic excellence. For more information, go to https://rhs.appstate.edu/ Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through inclusive practices, interprofessional collaboration, and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teach graduate courses related to occupation-based therapy; maintain expertise in areas of teaching responsibility Conduct and disseminate research in area of expertise and seek funding to support this research Collaborate with faculty in the MSOT program to ensure compliance with ACOTE accreditation and assist in collaborative program development including involvement in student recruitment and success Work with the program director to advance program sustainability and leadership Perform academic service appropriate for academic rank and professional or community-based service related to scholarly interests Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 FTE Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/09/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: No ABD consideration (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide with your application the following documents: Letter of Interest, Curriculum Vitae, Professional Reference List, Unofficial Transcripts, Teaching and Mentorship Philosophy, and Research Agenda. UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date 11/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Dr. Jennifer Howard Search Chair Email howardjs@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55953 Posting Number FA00603P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement on Teaching & Mentoring Philosophy Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56057": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Architectural Design &amp; Practice",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Architectural Design &amp; Practice Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Architectural Design & Practice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor in Building Sciences - emphasis in Architectural Design & Practice Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 098751 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Sustain Tech & Built Envir - 265300 Working Location (City, State) Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications A Master’s degree in Architecture is required by the time of hire; related fields may be considered. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Sustainable Technology & the Built Environment ( STBE ) houses three academic programs: the Bachelor of Science (BS) in Renewable Energy Technology; the BS in Building Sciences, with two concentrations; and the Master of Science in Technology. The Department includes more than 35 full-time faculty serving approximately 950 undergraduate and 30 graduate students. STBE has played an integral role in building the University’s sustainability agenda, which features prominently in the University’s Strategic Plan. Within STBE , faculty exemplify a commitment to applied research and interdisciplinary, experiential learning. Students in these programs have achieved notable successes in national and international competitions such as the Formula Sun Grand Prix and American Solar Challenge, the USDOE Race to Zero and Solar Decathlon, Solar Decathlon Europe, and the US EPA P3 program, among others. The Building Sciences Program is structured to establish a broad set of foundational skills and knowledge related to the whole life cycle of the built environment, including design, construction, and operations. This foundation acts as a catalyst for growth and success in our graduates’ careers. Extending beyond foundational principles, the program is committed to priming students’ minds to deconstruct, organize, and solve a wide range of problems related to the built environment in a team-based setting. Students go on to career paths in architecture, construction, building performance assessment, and facilities management. The College of Fine and Applied Arts ( CFAA ) at Appalachian State University is a dynamic, transdisciplinary academic unit that emphasizes experiential learning and offers 30 undergraduate degree programs, one graduate degree program and 13 minors through its seven member departments: Applied Design; Art; Communication; Military Science and Leadership; Sustainable Development; Sustainable Technology and the Built Environment; and Theatre and Dance (https://cfaa.appstate.edu/). Essential Duties and Responsibilities The primary responsibility of the position is teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Building Sciences program, which may include but are not limited to: 1. Architectural Design Studios, 2. Architectural Graphics and Modeling, 3. Sustainable Building Design and Construction, 4. Integrative Design Experiences ( IDEX ), 5. Virtual Design and Construction Other responsibilities include maintaining an active scholarly agenda, team-based coordination of a four-course studio sequence or building sciences integrated courses, advising students, collaborating with professionals in the building industry, and participating in service work. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position Typical physical demands of classroom and educational environments in a professional position at a university. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all below-required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s job board. Cover Letter / Letter of Interest that includes the following brief statements: ● Philosophy of instructional design ● Scholarly interests ● Commitment to sustainability ● Curriculum Vitae ● Sample of Architectural Design and/or Research Projects and/or Teaching Portfolio (max six pages) ● Unofficial Graduate Transcript(s) ● List of at least three (3) References with Contact Information ● Optional: License/Certification UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Dr. Sohad Abu-Elzait Search Chair Email abuelzaits@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55837 Posting Number FA00601P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Sample Projects (Explanation in Applicant Instructions) Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents License/Certification Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56041": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Lecturer Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Lecturer Position Number 0A1051 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Computer Information Systems - 255100 Working Location (City, State) Remote Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in a business-related field Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) A strong preference will be given to candidates with education in computer information systems or a related discipline, along with prior teaching experience in higher education and analytics with spreadsheet technology. It is also preferred that the successful candidate hold the MOS Excel Associate 365 Apps certification at the time of hire or commit to obtaining it within 60 days of employment (administered through the CIS department). Experience troubleshooting technical issues in computing environments is highly desirable. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to support students and faculty in technology-based learning and assessment settings. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Computer Information Systems is housed in the Walker College of Business https://business.appstate.edu/ at Appalachian State University. The Walker College of Business is committed to ensuring that its graduates are equipped to succeed in an increasingly innovative, multicultural, and interdependent world. Details about department programs and faculty/staff can be found at https://cis.appstate.edu/ . Essential Duties and Responsibilities This is a remote position with primary responsibility for teaching the introductory spreadsheet analytics course ( CIS 1060) in the Flight Path program . Each course assignment is delivered over an 8-week term, with the teaching assignment distributed across the academic year as follows: ● Fall 1: 2 courses ● Fall 2: 2 courses ● Spring 1: 2 courses ● Spring 2: 2 courses ● Summer: 2 courses The Lecturer will be expected to effectively use and manage technology platforms that support online instruction and assessment, using Canvas as the learning management system, GMetrix for exam preparation and assessment, Microsoft Excel and Microsoft 365, and other instructional and testing platforms that support student learning and certification activities. The Lecturer will also be expected to participate in service activities at the program, department, college, university, profession, and community levels, and responsibilities will include coaching and mentoring students. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 11 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants For a complete application, please apply and submit all required documents electronically through Appalachian State University’s Job Board: Cover letter Resume or Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for three references Evidence of successful teaching, such as teaching evaluations if prior classroom experience is indicated (attach under Evidence of Teaching) Statement of Teaching UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 09/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 09/16/2026 Search Chair Name Pranith Abbaraju Search Chair Email abbarajup@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55940 Posting Number FA00600P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Evidence of Teaching Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55935": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Position Number 095371 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Kinesiology - 273200 Working Location (City, State) Boone, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Kinesiology or a closely related discipline. Candidates whose degree is in a related discipline must demonstrate academic experience to be considered applicable for designation as Kinesiology faculty. Demonstrated potential to provide effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Record of scholarly productivity in Kinesiology or related discipline. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Demonstrated teaching expertise in one or more of the following areas: Exercise physiology, exercise prescription, sport and exercise nutrition, human anatomy and physiology, exercise psychology, behavior change, data analysis, and/or research methods CEP , EP, CSCS , CPSS , CMPC or other relevant credential A clearly articulated and impactful and fundable research agenda Evidence of ability to mentor students in scholarly endeavors and career advancement Evidence of service to the university, community, and/or professional organizations Evidence of post graduate education experience (postdoctoral or other professional) License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through inclusive practices, interprofessional collaboration, and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu The Department of Kinesiology comprises nationally accredited and recognized programs including a Bachelor of Science and Master of Science degree in Kinesiology (formerly Exercise Science). The Kinesiology graduate program at App State has a long history of success and prestige in strength & conditioning and clinical exercise physiology. The department features state-of-the-art laboratories and supports faculty with diverse research and practice backgrounds. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Kinesiology program (typically includes a 3:3 teaching load). Conducting and maintaining an active independent line of research in the discipline. Participating in service activities for the department, university, community, and professional organizations. Mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in research and scholarly activities. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/02/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit: Letter of Interest CV Professional Reference List Unofficial Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Kevin Zwetsloot Search Chair Email zwetslootka@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55799 Posting Number FA00599P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55866": {
      "title": "Practitioner in Residence for Department of Accounting",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Practitioner in Residence for Department of Accounting Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Practitioner in Residence for Department of Accounting Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Practitioner in Residence for Department of Accounting Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Practitioner in Residence Position Number 0A0571 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Accounting - 255050 Working Location (City, State) Remote Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in Accounting or closely related field. At least 10 years of relevant professional experience in Accounting or closely related field. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) The department is interested in candidates with several years of professional experience, in particular in the auditing or information systems field, with a professional certification (e.g., CPA or CMA ). License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Accounting has an enrollment of approximately 600 undergraduate majors across three campuses, Boone, Hickory, and online, and approximately 30 students seeking the M.S. degree. The department has 26 full-time faculty members. Additional information about the Department of Accounting can be found at accounting.appstate.edu. Essential Duties and Responsibilities This is an 11 month position that will primarily serve Appalachian State University’s online accounting program. Primary teaching duties will be upper level accounting courses online. Faculty members are expected to participate in service activities at the program, department, college, university, profession, and community levels. Responsibilities will also include coaching and mentoring students. Remote positions are considered for qualified candidates. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 11 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/04/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 08/31/2026 Search Chair Name Doug Roberts Search Chair Email robertsfd@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55690 Posting Number FA00598P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Interest List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
