      "title": "Lecturer in Professional Studies",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Lecturer in Professional Studies Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Lecturer in Professional Studies Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Lecturer in Professional Studies Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Provide Rank Lecturer Position Number 099311 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Rural Resilience and Innovations - 251000 Working Location (City, State) Hickory, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree from an accredited institution. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Candidates who can demonstrate the following are desired: Master’s Degree in Education or related field from an accredited institution. Strong interpersonal, collaborative, and communication skills. Teaching experience with adult learners and/or online, asynchronous teaching at the college level. Evidence of ability to advise and mentor students. License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit The Bachelor of Science in Professional Studies at App State is one of the university’s fastest growing degree programs and allows students to design their education by maximizing current career experience and prior college credits. Professional Studies is one of two programs in the Department of Rural Resilience and Innovation ( RRI ). RRI is one of 17 departments in the College of Arts and Sciences. The Professional Studies program emphasizes a breadth of study designed to strengthen high-demand workforce skills in management, leadership, technology and communication. Students benefit from faculty members across the university who understand a variety of professions and can give expert advice and guidance to advance students’ education and career. Professional Studies serves students at all three App State campuses: Boone, Hickory, and Online. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching and advising duties during the 9-month fall and spring academic year and 1 month advising duties during the summer. Teaching (50%-75% during fall and spring) Teach ”Foundations of Professional Studies”; “Capstone Internship” Primary teaching duties will be online asynchronous classes Teaching responsibilities will include 2-3 courses per semester (fall and spring). Online teaching is expected with potential for future in-person/hybrid courses. Fall: 2-3 sections of Foundations of Professional Studies Spring: 2-3 sections of Foundations of Professional Studies Potential for summer overload: Summer I or Summer II: 1 section of Foundations of Professional Studies and/or Capstone Internship for an overload in the summer Create and update curriculum materials to reflect advancements in the field. Student Advising Serve as advisor for Professional Studies students and assist Professional Studies director in internship coordination for the remainder of the teaching load each semester. Advise and mentor Professional Studies students, guiding them in their academic and career pursuits. Advise and mentor students for either Summer I or Summer II Service, Leadership, and Engagement Serve on department, college, and university committees The successful candidate will sincerely commit to promoting the College’s strategic Vision, Mission, and Values. For more information, click here . Participate in departmental and institutional committees and contribute to academic program development. Collaborate with colleagues on innovative projects and initiatives. Engage with the broader academic and professional communities through outreach and service. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 10 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 01/04/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: N/A - ABD is not applicable for this position. See Minimum Qualifications. ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date 11/27/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 11/04/2026 Search Chair Name Erin Lewis Search Chair Email lewismm4@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56505 Posting Number FA00619P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Statement on Teaching & Mentoring Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Evidence of Teaching Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56713": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Position Number 095371 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Kinesiology - 273200 Working Location (City, State) Boone, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Kinesiology or a closely related discipline. Candidates whose degree is in a related discipline must demonstrate academic experience to be considered applicable for designation as Kinesiology faculty. Demonstrated potential to provide effective teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Record of scholarly productivity in Kinesiology or related discipline. Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) Demonstrated teaching expertise in one or more of the following areas: Exercise physiology, exercise prescription, sport and exercise nutrition, human anatomy and physiology, exercise psychology, behavior change, data analysis, and/or research methods CEP , EP, CSCS , CPSS , CMPC or other relevant credential A clearly articulated and impactful and fundable research agenda Evidence of ability to mentor students in scholarly endeavors and career advancement Evidence of service to the university, community, and/or professional organizations Evidence of post graduate education experience (postdoctoral or other professional) License/Certification Required N/A Description of the Department or Unit Appalachian State University’s Beaver College of Health Sciences ( BCHS ) is transforming the health and quality of lives of individuals, families, and communities through inclusive practices, interprofessional collaboration, and innovation in teaching, scholarship, service, and clinical outreach. The BCHS supports over 3,400 students in ten undergraduate and ten graduate degree programs, organized into seven academic departments with 240 faculty and staff. The programs are located in Boone in the Holmes Convocation Center and the Leon Levine Hall of Health Sciences, the cornerstone of Boone’s Wellness District. We also have a clinical presence at the Hickory campus. The college supports the Appalachian Institute for Health and Wellness and has a collaborative partnership with the Wake Forest School of Medicine’s Physician Assistant Program and multiple health and human service agencies across the region. Learn more at https://healthsciences.appstate.edu The Department of Kinesiology comprises nationally accredited and recognized programs including a Bachelor of Science and Master of Science degree in Kinesiology (formerly Exercise Science). The Kinesiology graduate program at App State has a long history of success and prestige in strength & conditioning and clinical exercise physiology. The department features state-of-the-art laboratories and supports faculty with diverse research and practice backgrounds. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Kinesiology program (typically includes a 3:3 teaching load). Conducting and maintaining an active independent line of research in the discipline. Participating in service activities for the department, university, community, and professional organizations. Mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in research and scholarly activities. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 months Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions. Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/02/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: ABD with reduction in rank and salary (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit: Letter of Interest CV Professional Reference List Unofficial Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Research Agenda UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 11/03/2026 Open Until Filled No Evaluation of Applications Begins 10/01/2026 Search Chair Name Kevin Zwetsloot Search Chair Email zwetslootka@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/55799 Posting Number FA00599P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Undergraduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Transcript-Doctoral (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56704": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Statistics",
      "description": "Appalachian State University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Statistics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help AppState HR Home Page Veteran Recruitment Resources Assistant Professor of Statistics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Posting link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Application Deadline: All applications must be submitted electronically by 11:59 p.m. Eastern Time on the closing date indicated in the posting. For positions listed as Open Until Filled, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Request to Recruit Position Title Assistant Professor of Statistics Tenure Status Tenure Track Provide Rank Assistant Professor Position Number 047371 VISA Sponsorship? VISA sponsorship is available for this position. All candidates must be eligible to work and live in the U.S. Department Mathematical Sciences - 250500 Working Location (City, State) Boone, North Carolina Position Summary Information Minimum Qualifications The minimum qualifications include: an earned doctorate in statistics, biostatistics, data science or a closely related field with a minimum of 18 graduate hours of statistics coursework, a clear agenda for continuing scholarship, excellent written and verbal communication skills Areas of Interest and Preferred Qualifications (No Minimum Level Required) The department especially seeks someone with experience in or documented potential for the following: teaching core undergraduate and graduate-level courses in statistics, teaching advanced undergraduate and graduate-level elective courses, mentoring undergraduate and graduate-level student research projects, educating students of varied mathematical backgrounds, pursuing and implementing a variety of pedagogical strategies in the classroom, and supporting interdisciplinary programs and coursework. License/Certification Required Description of the Department or Unit The Department of Mathematical Sciences promotes intellectual curiosity, critical thinking, and a culture of learning in a supportive environment that encourages faculty to actively engage in teaching, scholarship, and service in the pursuit of student excellence. The department consists of 31 tenured or tenure track faculty and more than 30 full-time and part-time non-tenure track faculty. The department offers a B.S. degree in actuarial science and a B.S. degree in mathematics with concentrations in statistics, secondary education, business, life sciences, physical sciences, and computation. An undergraduate certificate is offered in sports analytics. The department also offers an M.A. with concentrations in either college teaching or secondary education. Over the last ten years, the department has graduated 55 undergraduate and 10 graduate majors each year on average. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Faculty in the Department of Mathematical Sciences will: teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the mathematical sciences, with a standard teaching load of 18 credit hours per year for research-active faculty, establish and maintain an active program of research or other scholarly activities that may include applying for external funding, participate in service activities which may include advising students, curriculum planning and assessment, working with professional organizations, and other activities needed for faculty governance at the department, college, and university levels, and provide support for the mathematical sciences community by encouraging the intellectual curiosity of students through undergraduate and graduate research projects and academic and career advising. Type of Position Full Time Position Appointment Type 1.0 Number Of Months Per Year 9 Physical Demands of Position To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential job duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions Posting Details Information Proposed Date of Hire 08/01/2027 Suggested Salary Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. ABD Consideration: No ABD consideration (see desc. below) ABD Description ABD with reduction in rank and salary: ABD will be considered for this position. Evidence of successful defense of the dissertation must be received by July 31 for a fall hire or November 30 for a spring hire. If confirmation of defense is not provided by the deadline, the candidate will receive a new one-year fixed-term contract and be hired at the rank of Instructor. The candidate’s salary will also be reduced to a lower rate commensurate with other full-time instructors in the same department. However, if degree verification is provided before the end of the one-year fixed-term contract, the candidate will be returned to the rank of assistant professor with commensurate compensation beginning July 1 of the following academic year. No ABD consideration: Only candidates with an earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution will be considered for the position. Since ABD will not meet the minimum requirements, ABD will not be considered. Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests UNC System Code (Section 610(2)) Special Faculty Hires The continued employment of a special faculty member during the term appointment may be made expressly contingent on items such as the continued availability of funding from any source, on enrollment levels, or any other contingency established by the institution. Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Evaluation of Applications Begins 01/15/2027 Search Chair Name Quinn A. Morris Search Chair Email morrisqa@appstate.edu Quick Link https://appstate.peopleadmin.com/postings/56622 Posting Number FA00616P Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References with Contact Information Transcript-Graduate (Unofficial) - No Password Protected Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Contact Us Why Work for AppState? University of North Carolina System Employment Careers with the State of North Carolina To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
